<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baga of Mauretania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baga was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauri">Mauri</a>, the first ruler of Mauretania known by name, in the late 3rd century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> records that in 206 BCE, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, he provided an escort of 4,000 Moorish warriors to the Numidian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a> on his way back to his kingdom. Nothing further is known of his reign.</p></div>
